---
title: Add a song
description: Add a song made in Mamar to your mod and play it with a SONG constant.
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

A song is a `.bgm` file in `audio/songs/`. You compose it in [Mamar](https://mamar.bates64.com), a music editor for Paper Mario, and the build names its `SONG_` constant after the file, so `meadow_theme.bgm` becomes `SONG_MEADOW_THEME`.

Mamar lists the instruments in the ROM you give it. To use instruments from a bank that your mod adds, build your mod and give Mamar `ver/us/build/papermario.z64` instead of the game's ROM.

## Add the song

1. In Mamar, compose your song, or open one of the game's songs, such as `audio/songs/pleasant_path.bgm`, as a starting point. Save the result as a `.bgm` file, such as `meadow_theme.bgm`.

    The file name must start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, digits, and underscores.

2. Copy the file to `audio/songs/meadow_theme.bgm`.

3. Rebuild the ROM. The build gives the song the constant `SONG_MEADOW_THEME`.

## Play the song

Use the constant in a map's music script:

```c
Call(SetMusic, 0, SONG_MEADOW_THEME, 0, VOL_LEVEL_FULL)
```

Load the map in the game to hear the song.

## Load extra sound banks with a song

Songs play instruments from the sound banks that are loaded when the song starts. Besides the banks that are always loaded, a song can load up to three song banks. A bank that any song loads is a song bank, and the game loads it only while such a song plays. For example, Toad Town's song loads `SPC0`.

To use an instrument from a song bank, choose it in Mamar's instrument list. Mamar loads the bank with the song and saves its name in the `.bgm` file, and the game loads the bank whenever it plays the song. If you start from one of the game's songs, its file already names the banks it needs.

A bank that a song loads isn't always loaded, so sound effects and ambient sounds can't play its samples. Mamar also lists the game's sound effect banks, such as `SYS0`, but if a song loads one of them, the build stops at the first sound effect that uses its samples. Choose instruments from the game's song banks, or from a bank you add for your songs.

## Replace a game song

To replace a song, save your version with the same file name in your layer, such as `audio/songs/toad_town.bgm`. It keeps the song's constant, so every map that plays the song uses your version.

## Remove a song

To remove a song, create `audio/songs/meadow_theme.bgm.meta` containing `delete: true`. The song's constant no longer exists, so the build fails if code still uses it. See [Fix audio build errors](/papermario-dx/audio/troubleshooting#compiler-errors-after-a-deletion).

## Limits

The game has room for 256 songs, and the build reports `there are more than 256 songs` if you add more.

